---
carb: other
tags:
- Contains-Dairy
- Contains-Gluten
- Vegetarian
method: stovetop
protein: none
ingredient_count: 5
---

Bring @water{4 1/2%cups} to boil in #medium saucepan{} over high heat.

Whisk in @coarse-ground polenta{1%cup}, @table salt{1%teaspoon}, and @baking soda{pinch}.

Bring mixture to boil, stirring frequently.

Reduce heat to lowest possible setting, cover, and cook for ~{5%minutes}.

Whisk until smooth; cover; and continue to cook until grains are tender but slightly al dente, about ~{25%minutes} longer. (Polenta should be loose and barely hold its shape when drizzled from #whisk{}; it will continue to thicken as it cools.)

Remove from heat, whisk in @unsalted butter{1%tablespoon} and @Parmesan cheese{1%ounce}(grated), and season with salt and pepper to taste.

Keep covered until ready to serve.